## Summary

Native schematic and PCB design in PCB Studio (`cadrs_eda`, no Bevy), worked through the KiCad course and checked against a real KiCad project.

- **Schematic:**
  - placing, wiring with automatic junctions, labels and global labels, text;
  - mirror, rotate while placing, copy/paste, find, net highlight;
  - wires stay on pins and square when parts move;
  - wire colours (a connected run changes together);
  - Choose… for a symbol's footprint;
  - plotting to PDF/SVG, netlist export;
  - wires on top of each other are joined after every edit, so they can't leave stray junction dots.
- **Layout:**
  - tracks, zones and keep-outs, lines/rectangles/circles/text, Import graphic (SVG onto any layer);
  - footprint and shape properties;
  - DRC, a layers panel, net highlighting, a ruler;
  - dragging footprints with the mouse;
  - lines and text drawn at their real width, so small pad text stays readable.
- **Libraries as data:**
  - symbols, footprints and 3D models in `libraries/`, made by `cadrs_libgen`;
  - a library browser;
  - parts downloaded from JLCPCB/EasyEDA (`cadrs_easyeda`) into the user's library folder.
- **3D:**
  - boards drawn in cadrs show their solder mask, copper, pads and silkscreen;
  - VRML/STEP/OBJ models with their colours;
  - the view orbits about the board after zoom to fit, or about the selected components;
  - outputs: STEP with models, JLCPCB BOM and placement files.
- **Documents page:**
  - PCB-only documents get a thumbnail of their board;
  - the details panel shows a 540×306 thumbnail (`thumbnail-large.png`) instead of the stretched 120×68 one.
- **Reference board:** the desk power monitor's LoRa board (`power_monitor`, scenario `pcbs_redraw`) is redrawn and checked against its KiCad files. Independent agent ratings of the match are 8.9–9.0/10 across schematic, layout and 3D.

## Testing

- `cargo test -r` and `cargo test -r --workspace -F cadrs/app-tests` pass. These include new unit tests for orbiting about a pivot, depth-centred zoom to fit, joining overlapping wires and junction colours, and the two thumbnail sizes.
- Clippy reports no new warnings in the changed code. Older warnings in other crates remain.
- **Golden screenshots (`--test golden -- --ignored`):**
  - The EDA goldens were reviewed and re-recorded locally (baselines aren't committed) for the board redraw. The last commit changes EDA line widths again, so they need recording again.
  - About 20 CAD goldens (assemblies, sketches, sheet metal) fail against local baselines dated 2026-10-06, before that day's merges from main. This branch doesn't touch those views. They need a separate look before being re-recorded.

