`camp_iterate_inventory` takes its online branch as soon as one of the camp's boxes has a game object (lines 774-781), and reads the other boxes through their server objects (816-841). Server objects export no uses, so that branch records every item in them with `uses = 1` (822, 831-833), and `consume_one_use` releases an item whose record says 1 (723, 738).

While the player is on the camp's level, one of those boxes always has a game object. `get_camp_containers` adds the hub's Hideout Furniture storage, `m_data.workshop_stashes[hub_id]` (643-651), which HF creates the first time the player opens the workbench's storage or workshop. HF's `GetStash` pins that `workshop_stash` online with `alife():set_switch_offline(id, false)`, and the engine then switches it online at any distance (`CSE_ALifeDynamicObject::try_switch_online`: `if (!can_switch_offline()) { alife().switch_online(this); return; }`). So while the player is on that level but out of switch range (450 m in G.A.M.M.A.), each multi-use item in the camp's other boxes goes whole on its first use:
- a settler's meal takes a whole 7-use `ration_ru`;
- a stove meal burns a whole 8-use `explo_jerrycan_fuel` or `explo_balon_gas`, or a 5-use `kerosene`;
- a Medkit order takes four vodkas (12 uses) for the 4 it needs;
- a pump batch takes a whole 3-use charcoal.

The 1-use records stay. Once the player changes level, #36's offline path reads them and releases those items whole as well.

This keeps the uses the camp last recorded for the same item: the online scan, `deposit_item_to_camp` and `consume_one_use` keep them current. #36's owed uses then apply in this branch too.

